; Level 1: the first of IO's four, and LEVEL1 on the disc, a level as the
; Level Designer saved it, its triggers named. src/level1.6502 and
; src/io.6502 make their bytes from this.
;
; How to read a level (leveldata.6502inc defines the notation and the
; names; level2.6502inc to level4.6502inc are written the same way). A
; level is a map of 64 x 64 cells, x across and y down from (0, 0) at the
; top left, and:
;
; - the player's start, and the exit. Once enough sulphur is collected the
;   player can light the exit (the pick-up key, P, facing it), and then has
;   four ticks of the clock to get five cells clear of it before it blazes.
; - 8 objects to pick up, carry in the backpack, use and throw. Each shows
;   an icon from the graphics set (default.6502inc), whose name the comment
;   gives.
; - 4 monsters: flames that move round the map, trying turns in their own
;   order at each step. Their cells count as fire, which kills.
; - 32 triggers (the Level Designer calls them puzzles). A trigger is a
;   place, or a whole row or column (IGNORE in a coordinate), that acts on
;   the level when the player walks onto it, or, with PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT,
;   when an object is used or lands there; object n can fire only triggers
;   n, n + 8, n + 16 and n + 24. Its condition byte can also ask for the
;   player to be facing a given way, or a given cell type in front (for a
;   thrown object, the way it flew and the cell it hit). Once fired it's
;   off (PUZZLE_OFF), unless PUZZLE_REUSABLE; one can start off, and other
;   triggers can turn it on and off. The action's arguments A, X and Y stay
;   in hex, as each action reads them its own way (PUZZLE_* in
;   leveldata.6502inc); the comment above each trigger says what it does in
;   the game. Triggers are numbered 0-31 here, as the game counts them; the
;   designer shows them one more.
;
; The map is 64 strings, a row each, a character a cell (MAP_KEY): "." the
; floor, "#" "=" and the corner pieces "r" "7" "L" "J" walls, "@" a
; barricade (another wall), "c" a crate, "o" sulphur, "~" lava, "+" "-" "|"
; pipes, "*" fire and "$" a cell holding an object (the start and the exit
; are marked so too).
level_1 = {
    ; The editing code, six digits: the Level Designer asks for it before it
    ; will edit the level, MISSION before it saves one of a locked mission's
    ; levels as a level file, and the game shows it once the level's done.
    "677636",
    ; The palette: the physical colours of logical colours 0-3, the "." and
    ; "1" to "3" the pictures are drawn in.
    {COLOUR_BLACK, COLOUR_BLUE, COLOUR_YELLOW, COLOUR_RED},
    ; The setup. The last byte picks, for cell types 5 (#), 8 (=), 7 (o)
    ; and A (~), two bits each from bit 7 down, which squares of a
    ; checkerboard show the type's second picture: none, the odd ones
    ; (x + y odd), the even ones or all (ALTERNATE_*).
    {
        62, 35,                         ; the player starts here
        124,                            ; sulphur to collect before the exit can be lit
        250,                            ; the clock's starting value
        31, 28,                         ; the exit
        CELL_SULPHUR * 16 + CELL_LAVA,  ; a monster meeting lava (~) turns it to sulphur (o) and is gone
        %00000111                       ; second pictures: o on odd squares, ~ on all
    },
    ; The objects: x, y, icon, then the number of uses plus OBJECT_* flags.
    {
        {32, 30, 0, OBJECT_NO_THROW + 2},                                        ; 0: Remote C.D.1
        {57, 15, 3, OBJECT_NO_CHARGES + OBJECT_NO_THROW + 2},                    ; 1: Blueprints
        {24, 30, 8, OBJECT_VANISHES + OBJECT_NO_THROW + 1},                      ; 2: Space Burger
        {31, 47, 13, OBJECT_NO_THROW + 1},                                       ; 3: Detonator
        {12, 48, 5, OBJECT_VANISHES + 1},                                        ; 4: Spanner
        {38, 46, 4, 10},                                                         ; 5: Mallet
        {54, 36, 2, OBJECT_NO_THROW + 3},                                        ; 6: Remote C.D.3
        {30, 38, 14, OBJECT_NO_CHARGES + OBJECT_VANISHES + OBJECT_NO_THROW + 1}  ; 7: Explosives
    },
    ; The monsters: x, y, the way each is going, and the order it tries
    ; turns in at each step (PATTERN_*, or four TURN_* fields, the first in
    ; bits 0-1, written out in the comment: "on" is straight on).
    {
        {45, 32, DIRECTION_UP, PATTERN_FOLLOW_EDGES},  ; 0
        {8, 31, DIRECTION_RIGHT, PATTERN_LEFT_WALL},   ; 1
        {1, 5, DIRECTION_UP, PATTERN_FOLLOW_EDGES},    ; 2
        {15, 3, DIRECTION_DOWN, PATTERN_FOLLOW_EDGES}  ; 3
    },
    ; The triggers: name, action (PUZZLE_*) and flags, where (x, y), the
    ; action's arguments A, X and Y, and the condition. The comment above
    ; each says what it does, then what the condition asks for.
    {
        ; 0: the cell at (31, 33) moves right; when facing down at a barricade (@)
        {"First Door", PUZZLE_MOVE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 31, 32, &01, &1F, &21, &F9},
        ; 1: takes the player to (31, 30)
        {"Telept Bck", PUZZLE_TELEPORT + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, IGNORE, IGNORE, &00, &1B, &1A, &00},
        ; 2: lets the player push 15 crates
        {"Strength  ", PUZZLE_PUSH_CRATES + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, IGNORE, IGNORE, &0F, &00, &00, &00},
        ; 3: blows up object 7; when facing a wall (=)
        {"Detonate  ", PUZZLE_DETONATE_OBJECT + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 31, IGNORE + 47, &07, &00, &1C, &48},
        ; 4: (7, 48) becomes a pipe across (-); when facing left at a pipe down (|)
        {"Boob Obj 1", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 6, 46, &0C, &07, &30, &CD},
        ; 5: the cell in front becomes the floor (.); when facing a crate (c)
        {"Hammer    ", PUZZLE_NEXT_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, IGNORE, IGNORE, &00, &00, &00, &46},
        ; 6: swaps the direction keys
        {"Puzzle 7  ", PUZZLE_DISORIENTATE + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT + PUZZLE_OFF, IGNORE, IGNORE, &15, &15, &15, &00},
        ; 7: turns on trigger 21; when facing up
        {"Tel Bck On", PUZZLE_TURN_ON + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 38, 9, &15, &15, &15, &A0},
        ; 8: takes the player to (47, 31); when facing right
        {"Telept Est", PUZZLE_TELEPORT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 22, 61, &00, &2B, &1B, &90},
        ; 9: sets the clock to 250; when facing left
        {"Recharge  ", PUZZLE_SET_LEVELS + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 30, 33, &01, &FA, &00, &80},
        ; 10: (7, 48) becomes a pipe across (-); when facing left at a pipe down (|)
        {"Boob obj 1", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 6, 46, &0C, &07, &30, &CD},
        ; 11: (31, 49) becomes a wall (=); when facing up
        {"Booby 1   ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 31, 48, &08, &1F, &31, &A0},
        ; 12: (9, 48) becomes a pipe across (-); when facing left at a pipe down (|)
        {"Boob Obj 2", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 6, 46, &0C, &09, &30, &CD},
        ; 13: takes the player to (31, 30); when facing up at lava (~)
        {"Real Start", PUZZLE_TELEPORT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, IGNORE + 24, 61, &00, &1B, &1A, &EA},
        ; 14: turns on trigger 15
        {"Monleap on", PUZZLE_TURN_ON + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 1, 59, &0F, &0F, &0F, &00},
        ; 15: pushes the cell in front to the player's left; when facing fire
        ; (*). (The designer stores a TURN_* times 4, so it would show &02 as
        ; backwards; but the game looks up &02 plus the way the player faces
        ; in its turns table, which for every facing gives the turn left.)
        {"Monleap   ", PUZZLE_MOVE_NEXT_BLOCK + PUZZLE_OFF + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, IGNORE, IGNORE, &02, &00, &00, &5E},
        ; 16: turns off triggers 15 and 21
        {"Monleap of", PUZZLE_TURN_OFF + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 31, 30, &0F, &15, &0F, &00},
        ; 17: (31, 47) becomes a wall (=); when facing up at the floor (.)
        {"Repl Obj 4", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 31, 48, &08, &1F, &2F, &E0},
        ; 18: throws object 4, 57 cells; when facing left
        {"Throw Obj ", PUZZLE_THROW_OBJECT, 11, 46, &04, &09, &39, &8D},
        ; 19: takes the player to (38, 10); when facing right
        {"Telept Et2", PUZZLE_TELEPORT + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, 19, 61, &00, &22, &06, &90},
        ; 20: the cell at (49, 0) moves right; when facing up
        {"One way 2 ", PUZZLE_MOVE_BLOCK, 51, 2, &01, &31, &00, &A0},
        ; 21: takes the player to (41, 7); when facing fire (*)
        {"Tel Bck   ", PUZZLE_TELEPORT + PUZZLE_OFF + PUZZLE_REUSABLE, IGNORE, IGNORE, &00, &25, &03, &4E},
        ; 22: (4, 16) becomes the floor (.); when facing right at a barricade (@)
        {"3rd door  ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 3, 16, &00, &04, &10, &D9},
        ; 23: (19, 47) becomes a pipe across (-); when facing down
        {"One way   ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 19, 53, &0C, &13, &2F, &B0},
        ; 24: the cell at (24, 53) moves left; when facing down at a barricade (@)
        {"2nd door  ", PUZZLE_MOVE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 24, 52, &00, &18, &35, &F9},
        ; 25: puts monster 0 at (42, 9) going right, back and forth; when facing up
        {"Relocate  ", PUZZLE_PLACE_MONSTER, 49, 25, &A8, &B1, &25, &A0},
        ; 26: (41, 0) becomes lava (~); when facing right
        {"Order 1   ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 41, 4, &0A, &29, &00, &90},
        ; 27: (43, 0) becomes lava (~); when facing right
        {"Order 2   ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 43, 5, &0A, &2B, &00, &90},
        ; 28: (45, 0) becomes lava (~); when facing right
        {"Order 3   ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 45, 5, &0A, &2D, &00, &90},
        ; 29: (47, 0) becomes lava (~); when facing right
        {"Order 4   ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 47, 4, &0A, &2F, &00, &90},
        ; 30: (40, 10) becomes the floor (.); when facing down at a barricade (@)
        {"4th door  ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK + PUZZLE_USES_OBJECT, 40, 9, &00, &28, &0A, &F9},
        ; 31: (61, 2) becomes a barricade (@); when facing right
        {"One way 3 ", PUZZLE_PLACE_BLOCK, 59, 0, &09, &3D, &02, &90}
    },
    ; The map: 64 rows of 64 cells, in MAP_KEY's characters.
    {
        "~=.~~~~~~~=====~~~~~~~=~~~~=~~~.--+..#o..........@..-----------+",
        "~........=.............==o.....=o.|7r#|----------|..LLL**...*or|",
        "...~~~~~.=.o.====.7r7r.=..=.==.==o|JL#|....c...o.|r|......o*..r|",
        "~.~r##7~.=..o..*=.LJLJ.=..=.==....|..#|..*.o.~.c.|r|.....*..*.r|",
        "~.~####~.=....=.=......=..=.==..=.|7r#|..o.c.*...|r|**..*...*.r|",
        "~*~####~.======.====...=..=.==..=.|JLJ|-.*...o.c..r|.....*....r|",
        "~.~L##J=...........===.o..=...===.|..~-|----------r|.....*..*.r|",
        "~.~~=~~==.=====.==.....=..=.....=.|7r7................*...*...-+",
        "=....=.......==.==.o.o.=..=o==..o.|JL#o..|===|===|==*..**....*~=",
        "~=o=....===............=..=o==....|..J.=.|......$o$~=*~~~=~*===.",
        "~===.==o====..=.==.o.o==..=====.=.|7r..=@|=========+---------|.|",
        "=..........==.=.==.=.===...==oo.=.|JL--=o+-+.......|.........|.-",
        "=.r7..~~~~.==......=.=.....==o=.o.|..|.------------++--------+..",
        "=.LJ.~~~.~...o...===.=.===.====.=.|7r..+----+.......|...r..7.|.|",
        "=....=~~|=.............oo=........|..|.|..+---------+..rJ..L7+-+",
        "~=..=o~~|~.~~~~..===o=======ooo.==+--+c|cc|||..r.7....rJr$.7L7..",
        "~oo.@o~~|~.o..=.................==...|....|||.rJ|L7..rJrJ..L7L7.",
        "~...~~~~|~~~~~~=o=~~~~=.=o-----+==.+-+.o..--+r.-+-o##JrJr..7L7L7",
        "~~~~~~+-+|-------------|----------+|+-....||r###|####.JrJ..L7L.#",
        "~+----|----------+~~~+-|----------|+|c....||#J..|L###..........#",
        "~|~~~~|.....|~~~~|~~~|.....|-..-.-|-+c|c-c||#7....##=.======.==~",
        "~.----+.---|-----|---+.+---------.+---|--+||#####.##=.=......=.~",
        "~=====~====.|--------+.|.......|..+---+.||||#.oc#.##=.=.oooo.=.~",
        "=..o..=.=..=....=|J.L|.+-------|--|----+||||#.c...##=.=.o..o.=.~",
        "=.===.=....=..=.=|...|.|****.......====|||||#...#.##=.=.oooo.=.~",
        "=.=...==..=.....=|...|.|**...........==|||+-.####.##=........=.~",
        "=.=.===.....oo..=|...|.|*.............=|||||#o.o..##=.========.~",
        "=.=...=.oo=....==|...|.|*..@.......~..=|||||#$$$$~##=.------+=.~",
        "=.===.=.......=.=|7.r|.|......r$7......|||||.oo.o@##========|=.~",
        "=.=.$.=...o.=...=+-+=|||.....rJ.L7......|||||.....##=......=|=.~",
